ENTRY            D6522   20260818   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D6522001   20260818   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 10         25
TITLE      Experimental insights into entrance channel
            parameters for the 19F+93Nb system: signature of
            incomplete fusion
AUTHOR     (A.K.Jashwal, A.Agarwal, H.Vardhan, M.Kumar, K.Kumar,
            S.Dutt, M.F.Khan, I.A.Rizvi, A.K.Chaubey)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRIMP,3INDMUA)
           (3INDIND) Bareilly College, Bareilly, U.P
           (3INDIND) Hindu College, Moradabad, U.P.
           (3INDIND) KCMT, Bareilly, U.P
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,113,034615,2026)
           #doi:10.1103/4sbt-4whn
FACILITY   (VDGT,3INDNSD) 15UD pelletron accelerator
SAMPLE     Three stacks of 93Nb self-supported thin targets
            having thickness ~1.5-1.6 mg/cm2 backed by Al foils
            of thickness from 1.4-1.6 mg/cm2 were prepared by a
            rolling technique.
DETECTOR   (HPGE)
METHOD     (ACTIV,STTA) Three stacks have been separately
            irradiated for about ~8-9 hr.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) The overall uncertainties are estimated <=16%.
            The determination of geometry-dependent efficiency
            also add some uncertainty in measured cross section:
           (ERR-1,,2.) thickness of target foils (<2%)
           (ERR-2,,6.) fluctuations in the beam current (<6%.)
HISTORY    (20260818C) A.Gandhi
ENDBIB              25
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           28
